erity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"app/javascript/firebase_auth.js\",\n      \"line\": \"30-48\",\n      \"description\": \"CSRF token dependency on meta tag without fallback validation. While the approach is sound, missing CSRF token would silently fail without clear error messaging.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 42,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"Add MIME type validation: Check file.type against whitelist (application/pdf, image/jpeg, etc.) before processing. Example: `if (!file.type.match(/^(application\\\\/pdf|image\\\\/(jpeg|png|webp))$/)) { return alert('Invalid file type'); }`\",\n    \"Implement file size limits: Enforce maximum file sizes before processing. Example: `const MAX_SIZE = 50 * 1024 * 1024; if (file.size > MAX_SIZE) { alert('File too large'); return; }`\",\n    \"Replace external CDN with local bundle: Self-host the PDF.js worker or use a trusted, pinned version from node_modules instead of relying on esm.run CDN\",\n    \"Sanitize error messages: Filter sensitive details from user-facing error messages. Keep detailed errors in console only: `alert('Processing failed. Please try again.'); console.error('Details:', error);`\",\n    \"Add file header magic number validation: Verify file signatures (PDF magic bytes: 0x25504446) before processing to confirm actual file type\",\n    \"Implement request timeouts: Add timeouts to file processing operations to prevent indefinite hanging\",\n    \"Review Firebase Security Rules: Ensure Firestore/Realtime Database rules properly restrict data access (not shown in provided code)\",\n    \"Enable Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Restrict script sources to prevent injection attacks and external resource loading\",\n    \"Update dependencies**: Check for known vulnerabilities in pdf-lib, jsPDF, and other dependencies using `npm audit` or similar tools\",\n    \"Store sensitive config server-side**: Move Firebase config to server-side environment variables when possible, only expose public keys to fronte